<section class="fh5co-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
        <p>For ten years we've gathered online and on conference stages to ask one question together: what does it mean to follow Christ into the future? This fall, we're doing something we've never done — going <em>away</em> together. Three days on 300 wooded acres: a lake, trails, a chapel, fire and conversation late into the night.</p>
        <p>This is a retreat, not a conference. Fewer talks, more table. We'll come to embody the thing we keep pointing at — a hopeful, rational, future-facing faith — before we argue another word about it.</p>
        <p>The theme that will hold our weekend: <strong>the shape of progress is the face of Christ.</strong> Come find out what we mean.</p>
        <p>We work against illness, hunger, oppression, injustice, and death — and once a year, it's good to do that work shoulder to shoulder, in person, with people who see what you see.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="fh5co-section" style="background: #f7f7f7;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
